  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "You’d now like to experiment to see if the neural network’s performance improves with more training iterations. This program includes a loop that trains a new neural network four times, allowing it 1, 10, 50 and 100 iterations over the items.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Run the program. It trains a network for 1 and 10 iterations. How accurate is the network on your three test items each time?\r\n- Change the list of `max_iter` values so the program also tries 50, then 100. Run it each time. How does the model's accuracy change as you increase the number of iterations? At which `max_iter` does the network get every item right?\r\n- Add one more value of your own, at least 200. Predict what you think will happen, then run it. Was your prediction right?\r\n- Compare the results with your predictions in Level 1. Look at the Small Jar. Why might the network you trained in Level 1 get the Small Jar wrong?\r\n\r\nYou'll answer questions about this output in the next level.\r\n",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
